;
; DEED clause profile: (rsr-scorecard …), v0.2.0
; Prose and rationale: 1-formats/deed/mappings/scorecard-corpus-decision.adoc
; section 6 (the RSR scorecard). Owner ruling 2026-11-14: a new RSR scorecard
; clause carrying the tier, the score and the per-criterion results, which the
; oracle (Hypatia RsrConformance, `mix hypatia.rsr_score --write`) writes in
; place of .machine_readable/scorecards/rsr.scorecard.a2ml. Ratified by the
; owner on 2026-11-14 (superseding R5 option B), with :assessor and
; :assessed-at added.
;
; CHANGELOG (v0.1.0 DRAFT → v0.2.0, owner ratification 2026-11-14):
;   - Two required fields, each exactly once: :assessor, the tool that
;     produced the scorecard (a non-empty string such as
;     "hypatia rsr_score 0.1.0"), and :assessed-at, when it ran, an RFC 3339
;     UTC timestamp string (sc-timestamp). Not additive: a v0.1.0 scorecard
;     without them is refused, and is rewritten by rescoring.
;   - The date in :assessed-at is common.abnf's date, borrowed, not restated.
;   - The profile is no longer marked DRAFT.
;
; A CLAUSE PROFILE, not a new grammar. Every rule below is also a `field` or
; `clause` of deed.abnf v2.0.0, so a deed carrying one still passes deed_lint
; unchanged, and no file name or doc-head is added. Rules it borrows (string,
; boolean, token-sep, hex-lc, DQUOTE, DIGIT) are deed.abnf's, and date is
; common.abnf's, all unchanged.
; Requires RFC 7405 (%s"..." case-sensitive string literals).
;
; Where it appears: exactly one (rsr-scorecard …) clause, at the top level of a
; praxis-deed whose :profile is the symbol rsr-scorecard, conventionally
; .machine_readable/scorecards/rsr-scorecard_praxis.deed in the scored repo.
; A scorecard is an assessment record, neither identity (the chora deed) nor
; content organisation (CLADE.deed) nor registry (chora-registry), so it is
; never a clause of a repo-deed; it follows the proof receipt (PROOF-POLICY
; 8.5), the other machine-written verification record, which is a praxis-deed
; profile too. SEMANTIC (validator-enforced, deed_lint.js --rsr-scorecard):
;   * the praxis-deed's top level carries :schema-version, :canonical-name and
;     :profile rsr-scorecard, at most :beholding-chora besides, and the one
;     clause; an (rsr-scorecard …) anywhere else is refused;
;   * :repo, :spec, :spec-version, :assessor, :assessed-at, :tier, :score,
;     :provisional and :automatable-coverage exactly once; the other fields
;     at most once;
;   * :assessor is not empty, and the date in :assessed-at is a real
;     calendar date (2026-02-31 is refused), as common.abnf's date says;
;   * at least one (criterion …); in each, every crit-field exactly once;
;     :id unique across the clause;
;   * :score is at most 100, and :automatable-coverage at most 1;
;   * :provisional is #t when :automatable-coverage is below 1, and a
;     provisional scorecard is never rhodium (RSR-SPEC-v2 section 10: no firm
;     tier claim from partial coverage);
;   * :score is derived, not asserted: it equals 100 times the passed weight
;     (pass counts whole, partial half) over the verified weight (pass,
;     partial and fail), within 0.02 for the rounding of the weights, and is
;     "0" when nothing is verified;
;   * :automatable-coverage likewise equals the verified weight over the
;     applicable weight (every verdict but na), within 0.001;
;   * :applicable-weight and :verified-weight, when present, equal those sums
;     within 0.01.

rsr-scorecard-clause = "(" %s"rsr-scorecard" 1*(token-sep sc-member) [token-sep] ")"
sc-member       = sc-field / sc-criterion

sc-field        = ( %s":repo"                 token-sep string )
                / ( %s":spec"                 token-sep %s"rsr-criteria-v2" )
                / ( %s":spec-version"         token-sep string )
                / ( %s":assessor"             token-sep string )
                / ( %s":assessed-at"          token-sep sc-timestamp )
                / ( %s":tier"                 token-sep sc-tier )
                / ( %s":score"                token-sep sc-decimal )
                / ( %s":provisional"          token-sep boolean )
                / ( %s":automatable-coverage" token-sep sc-decimal )
                / ( %s":applicable-weight"    token-sep sc-decimal )
                / ( %s":verified-weight"      token-sep sc-decimal )
                / ( %s":profile-present"      token-sep boolean )
                / ( %s":source-commit"        token-sep DQUOTE 40hex-lc DQUOTE )
                ; :repo is the scored repo's name (its chora deed's
                ; :canonical-name when it has one). :spec names the criteria
                ; family as a symbol; :spec-version is the catalogue's own
                ; version string, verbatim. :source-commit is the scored
                ; commit, when the writer was told it. :assessor names the
                ; tool that produced the scorecard and its version, such as
                ; "hypatia rsr_score 0.1.0"; :assessed-at is when it ran.

sc-timestamp    = DQUOTE date %s"T" sc-hour ":" sc-minute ":" sc-second %s"Z" DQUOTE
sc-hour         = ( "0" / "1" ) DIGIT / "2" %x30-33
sc-minute       = %x30-35 DIGIT
sc-second       = %x30-35 DIGIT
                ; RFC 3339 date-time in UTC, written one way: an upper-case T
                ; and Z, whole seconds, no fraction, no numeric offset, and no
                ; leap second (60), which no writer emits. For example
                ; "2026-11-14T19:33:12Z". date is common.abnf's (YYYY-MM-DD).

sc-tier         = %s"none" / %s"bronze" / %s"silver" / %s"gold" / %s"rhodium"
crit-tier       = %s"bronze" / %s"silver" / %s"gold" / %s"rhodium"
sc-verdict      = %s"pass" / %s"partial" / %s"fail" / %s"unverified" / %s"na"
                ; Symbols, matched whole: each is followed by token-sep or ")".

sc-decimal      = DQUOTE 1*DIGIT [ "." 1*DIGIT ] DQUOTE
                ; deed.abnf has no decimal literal, so a decimal is a string
                ; of this shape: "84.08", "0.73", "1".

sc-criterion    = "(" %s"criterion" 1*(token-sep crit-field) [token-sep] ")"
crit-field      = ( %s":id"      token-sep DQUOTE crit-id DQUOTE )
                / ( %s":name"    token-sep string )
                / ( %s":tier"    token-sep crit-tier )
                / ( %s":gate"    token-sep string )
                / ( %s":weight"  token-sep sc-decimal )
                / ( %s":verdict" token-sep sc-verdict )
crit-id         = 1*DIGIT 1*( "." 1*DIGIT )
                ; The criterion's id in the catalogue, e.g. "3.1.1". :gate is
                ; the capability that makes it applicable ("universal" or a
                ; capability name), verbatim from the catalogue.
